Same two channels, straight off an ESP32. Declare the fields once, then log a row per control loop.

```cpp
#include <AlloyLogger.h>
AlloyLogger alloy;

void setup() {
  alloy.wifi("your-ssid", "your-password");
  alloy.begin("warehouse-rover", "your-device-key");
  alloy.describe("/drive", "vel", "m/s");
  alloy.describe("/drive", "current", "A");
  alloy.describe("/sys", "temp", "C");
}

void loop() {
  alloy.log("/drive").set("vel", readVelocity()).set("current", readCurrent());
  alloy.log("/sys").set("temp", readDriverTemp());
  alloy.end();
}
```

That is the whole integration. The mission you are looking at now is the same shape of data.
